# Package boundaries (Handbook §1.8, §5.4 — enforced by tests/architecture/)

The architecture is frozen. Implement inside it; never propose a redesign,
move packages around, or add a new package taxonomy in this repo.

Real, current allowed import edges (see
`apps/backend/tests/architecture/test_dependencies.py` — the actual source
of truth; this rule summarizes it):

- `services/voice`, `services/calendar`, `services/automation` — leaves.
  Import nothing from `memory`, `runtime`, or another service.
- `services/knowledge` -> `memory`, `services.brain` only.
- `services/brain` -> `memory` only. **Only this package may call the
  Claude API** (no `ANTHROPIC_API_URL` / `x-api-key` anywhere else).
- `services/planner` -> `memory`, `services.calendar` only.
- `services/api` -> `memory`, `runtime`, `services.brain`, `services.calendar`,
  `services.planner`. Nothing may import `services.api` back.
- `memory` -> stdlib / `sqlite3` / `lancedb` only. **Only `memory/semantic/`
  imports `lancedb`.** No other package opens a DB connection.
- `identity`, `paths`, `conversation_memory`, `memory_producers` are
  dependency-free root utilities any package may import.

If the change you're making needs an edge not listed above, stop and say so
explicitly — do not add the import and do not silently work around the rule
(e.g. re-implementing the same logic locally to avoid the import is also a
violation of intent). This is a human/ADR decision.

Every write is a `MutationEvent` built in `runtime/mutation_builders.py` and
applied via `runtime/side_effects.finalize_mutations()` — never persist by
calling `memory.*` write functions directly from a service or router.

Run `python -m pytest apps/backend/tests/architecture/` after any import
change — it is the fastest way to know if you crossed a boundary.
